Vulnerability: Information Disclosure Through Verbose IIS Error Messages
Suggested severity: Low
CWE: CWE-209 – Generation of Error Message Containing Sensitive Information
OWASP Top 10: A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration
CVSS v3.1: 3.7 (Low) — CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N
Vulnerability description
The application displays detailed Microsoft IIS error messages when an invalid URL is requested. The error response reveals internal server information, including the physical directory path, IIS modules, handler details, error codes, and Windows authentication information.

Exposing such internal implementation details may assist an attacker in understanding the application's server environment and identifying potential attack vectors.
Impact
An attacker who can access these error messages may obtain information about the application's internal directory structure, Windows environment, and request-handling configuration.

This information could assist in developing more targeted attacks, such as path traversal or file-handling attacks. However, the disclosed information does not independently demonstrate unauthorized file access or compromise.
Mitigation
Configure IIS to display generic error pages to remote users and prevent detailed diagnostic information from being exposed in HTTP responses. Enable appropriate httpErrors and customErrors settings, restrict detailed errors to authorized administrators, and maintain detailed diagnostic information only in protected server-side logs.
Proof of Concept (PoC)
Step 1: Open the application in a browser and navigate to an invalid URL:
http://mip-decryptionservice.webfarm-uat.ms.com/@


Step 2: Observe that the application returns an HTTP 404.0 detailed IIS error page exposing:
- Physical server directory path (d:\inetpub\uat\...)
- IIS module: IIS Web Core
- Handler: StaticFile
- Error code: 0x80070002
- Windows logon method and user account information
Observed result: Internal server configuration details are disclosed through the HTTP error response instead of a generic error page.

